Q:

HTTP/1.1 405 Method Not Allowed as a respond

I try https://developer.atlassian.com/jiradev/jira-apis/jira-rest-apis/jira-rest-api-tutorials/jira-rest-api-example-edit-issues with my own credentials
curl -D- -u fred:fred -X PUT --data {see below} -H "Content-Type: application/json" http://kelpie9:8081/rest/api/2/issue/QA-31

but it throws an error as HTTP/1.1 405 Method Not Allowed
what can be the problem?

A:

The document that you mentioned clearly said that, it's applicable for JIRA 5.0 and later. So most likely that old version of JIRA doesn't have this method :-)
As far as I can remember JIRA 4.2.1 has Alpha version of REST API thus if you really wants to use REST API better to consider upgrading your JIRA to the latest version. I believe this call is not supported for your current version.

Downgrading Your Version of WordPress

I don’t recommend this, but sometimes you’ll update the core and a theme or plugin will break and you need some time for the developer to catch up. Keep in mind that downgrading your site leaves your site vulnerable to hacking, so if the plugin/theme isn’t updated soon, then you will need to find a new theme/plugin. This video shows the easiest way to do it using FTP.Q:

adding clickable image links to jquery code

i show some images with the simple script shown below. how can i make the images clickable?
thank you!
$(function() {
    $('.fadein img:gt(0)').hide();     
    setInterval(function() {
        $('.fadein :first-child').fadeOut().next('img').fadeIn().end().appendTo('.fadein');
    }, 4000);
});

A:

$(function() {
    $('.fadein img:gt(0)').hide();
    $('.fadein img:gt(0)').click(function() {
      window.location.href = 'http://www.google.com';
    });
    setInterval(function() {
        $('.fadein :first-child').fadeOut().next('img').fadeIn().end().appendTo('.fadein');
    }, 4000);
});

